load @term/seed/space/hyperbolic/heptagrid
  find heptagrid

# The mantilla, the recursive lace-like pattern that lives in the heptagrid {7, 3}, a background of nested regions of
# interwoven triangles that a clever tile set can be forced to build. The mantilla encodes a hierarchy capable of
# simulating any computation, and it is the structure at the heart of Margenstern's solution of the hyperbolic tiling
# problem: whether a given finite set of tiles can tile the hyperbolic plane is UNDECIDABLE, a theorem independently
# confirmed by Kari in 2007. The form carries the heptagrid the mantilla is built in.
form mantilla
  link grid, like heptagrid
